      "country": "Argentina, Denmark, Mexico, United States of America, Netherlands, France",
      "country_zh": null,
      "runtime": 119,
      "language": "ES",
      "synopsis_en": "In 2009, a man and two accomplices try to evict members of the Indigenous community of Chuschagasta in northern Argentina. Claiming ownership of the land and armed with guns, they kill the community’s leader, Javier Chocobar. The murder is caught on video. It takes nine years of protests before court proceedings are finally opened in 2018. During all this time, the killers remain free. The film combines the voices and photographs of the community with courtroom footage to explore the long history of colonialism and land dispossession that led to this crime.",
      "synopsis_zh": "2009年，阿根廷北部，一名男子伙同两名帮凶试图驱逐丘斯卡加斯塔原住民社区的成员。他们持枪宣称拥有土地所有权，杀害了社区领袖哈维尔·乔科瓦尔。谋杀过程被视频记录下来。经过长达九年的抗议，法院才于2018年开庭审理此案。在此期间，凶手一直逍遥法外。影片结合社区民众的声音、照片以及法庭影像资料，探寻导致这场罪行的殖民主义与土地剥夺的漫长历史。",
      "poster_url": "https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/1gXQmNpaKvjskAxfHWwdpK4IeHN.jpg",
